    {
      "question": "e-85",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "1dd5b29706620ca68aa5e98b90918fdb1473e69d36ba9c2f6d7bbffb6b871db5",
      "new_sha256": "7e0e956a613f35937ec81c1f199268a49c791fa447e34f791d4b04e45cfcf165",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-85",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-6}{{x}^{2}-5x+6} & =\\frac{(x-2)(x+3)}{(x-2)(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x+3)}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+3}{x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-3 = 0\\qquad \\Longrightarrow\\qquad x=3.\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=3.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979852/example-85.json",
          "file_sha256": "47f9679b2dcbc996329e4258448b7d53d0b970cfdd7a86bdfb696b8c2f8ecc24"
        }
