    {
      "question": "e-86",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "1a505ba41447427c98f121dab12a394f86910a61a35d65243744282df229236c",
      "new_sha256": "d0e95530cfb52b277fac16a8764011168d197c23395293ec8763c2ce98288e10",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-86",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x}{2x+2} & =\\frac{x(x+1)}{2(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\cancel{(x+1)}}{2\\cancel{(x+1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979852/assets/eda5457edafe14fb51fcc75ca75677b199bfc3e0aef8940c66f8aa78cf8cd5c3.png)",
